{"id":"mahabharata-1-187","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":187,"title":"सप्ताशीत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 187 · Yudhishthira reveals himself; the question of five husbands","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira tells Drupada who they are, to his great joy, but declares that Draupadi must be the wife of all five brothers. Drupada protests that one woman with many husbands is unheard of; as they argue, Vyasa arrives.","kn":"ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ತಾವು ಯಾರೆಂದು ದ್ರುಪದನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಅವನು ಅತ್ಯಾನಂದಪಡುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಆದರೆ ದ್ರೌಪದಿ ಐವರು ಸಹೋದರರ ಪತ್ನಿಯಾಗಬೇಕೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಒಬ್ಬ ಸ್ತ್ರೀಗೆ ಅನೇಕ ಪತಿಗಳು ಎಂದೂ ಕೇಳಿಲ್ಲವೆಂದು ದ್ರುಪದನು ಆಕ್ಷೇಪಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಚರ್ಚೆ ನಡೆಯುತ್ತಿರುವಾಗ ವ್ಯಾಸರು ಬರುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर द्रुपद को अपना परिचय देते हैं, जिससे वे अत्यन्त प्रसन्न होते हैं, पर कहते हैं कि द्रौपदी पाँचों भाइयों की पत्नी होगी। द्रुपद आपत्ति करते हैं कि एक स्त्री के अनेक पति अनसुनी बात है; विवाद के बीच व्यास आ पहुँचते हैं।","te":"యుధిష్ఠిరుడు తామెవరో ద్రుపదునికి చెబుతాడు, అతడు అమితానందం పొందుతాడు; కానీ ద్రౌపది ఐదుగురు సోదరులకు భార్య కావాలంటాడు. ఒక స్త్రీకి అనేకులు భర్తలనేది ఎన్నడూ వినలేదని ద్రుపదుడు అభ్యంతరపెడతాడు; చర్చ జరుగుతుండగా వ్యాసుడు వస్తాడు.","ta":"யுதிஷ்டிரர் தாம் யாரென்று த்ருபதனிடம் சொல்ல, அவன் பெருமகிழ்ச்சி அடைகிறான்; ஆனால் திரௌபதி ஐந்து சகோதரர்களுக்கும் மனைவியாக வேண்டும் என்கிறார். ஒரு பெண்ணுக்குப் பல கணவர் என்பது கேள்விப்படாதது என்று த்ருபதன் மறுக்க, விவாதத்தின்போது வியாஸர் வருகிறார்.","ml":"താൻ ആരാണെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ദ്രുപദനോട് പറയുന്നു; അദ്ദേഹത്തിന് വലിയ സന്തോഷമാകുന്നു. എന്നാൽ ദ്രൗപദി അഞ്ചു സഹോദരന്മാരുടെയും ഭാര്യയായിരിക്കണമെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ പ്രഖ്യാപിക്കുന്നു. ഒരു സ്ത്രീക്ക് പല ഭർത്താക്കന്മാർ എന്നത് കേട്ടുകേൾവിയില്ലാത്തതാണെന്ന് ദ്രുപദൻ എതിർക്കുന്നു; അവർ തർക്കിക്കുമ്പോൾ വ്യാസൻ എത്തുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.187; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"वैवाहिकपर्व","titleEn":"Vaivahika Parva (The wedding)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तत आहूय पाञ्चाल्यो राजपुत्रं युधिष्ठिरम् ।\nपरिग्रहेण ब्राह्मेण परिगृह्य महाद्युतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the radiant Panchala king called the prince Yudhishthira and received him with the welcome given to a Brahmin."}},{"n":2,"text":"पर्यपृच्छददीनात्मा कुन्तीपुत्रं सुवर्चसम् ।\nकथं जानीम भवतः क्षत्रियान्ब्राह्मणानुत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The unwavering king asked the splendid son of Kunti: How are we to know whether you are Kshatriyas or Brahmins,"}},{"n":3,"text":"वैश्यान्वा गुणसंपन्नानुत वा शूद्रयोनिजान् ।\nमायामास्थाय वा सिद्धांश्चरतः सर्वतोदिशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"or accomplished Vaishyas, or born of Shudras, or perhaps perfected beings who have taken on a disguise and wander in every direction,"}},{"n":4,"text":"कृष्णाहेतोरनुप्राप्तान्दिवः संदर्शनार्थिनः ।\nब्रवीतु नो भवान्सत्यं संदेहो ह्यत्र नो महान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"come for Krishna's sake, wanting to see the heavens? Tell us the truth, for we have great doubt about this."}},{"n":5,"text":"अपि नः संशयस्यान्ते मनस्तुष्टिरिहाविशेत् ।\nअपि नो भागधेयानि शुभानि स्युः परंतप ॥","meaning":{"en":"May our minds find contentment at the end of this doubt, and may our fortunes be auspicious, scorcher of foes."}},{"n":6,"text":"कामया ब्रूहि सत्यं त्वं सत्यं राजसु शोभते ।\nइष्टापूर्तेन च तथा वक्तव्यमनृतं न तु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Out of kindness tell the truth, for truth adorns kings; by sacrifices and good works too one must not speak falsehood."}},{"n":7,"text":"श्रुत्वा ह्यमरसंकाश तव वाक्यमरिंदम ।\nध्रुवं विवाहकरणमास्थास्यामि विधानतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing your word, godlike subduer of foes, I will certainly undertake the wedding rites according to rule."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":8,"text":"मा राजन्विमना भूस्त्वं पाञ्चाल्य प्रीतिरस्तु ते ।\nईप्सितस्ते ध्रुवः कामः संवृत्तोऽयमसंशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Do not be troubled, Panchala king; may you be glad. This wish of yours has surely come true, without doubt."}},{"n":9,"text":"वयं हि क्षत्रिया राजन्पाण्डोः पुत्रा महात्मनः ।\nज्येष्ठं मां विद्धि कौन्तेयं भीमसेनार्जुनाविमौ ।\nयाभ्यां तव सुता राजन्निर्जिता राजसंसदि ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, we are Kshatriyas, sons of the great-souled Pandu. Know me as Kunti's eldest, and these two as Bhimasena and Arjuna, by whom your daughter was won in the royal assembly."}},{"n":10,"text":"यमौ तु तत्र राजेन्द्र यत्र कृष्णा प्रतिष्ठिता ।\nव्येतु ते मानसं दुःखं क्षत्रियाः स्मो नरर्षभ ।\nपद्मिनीव सुतेयं ते ह्रदादन्यं ह्रदं गता ॥","meaning":{"en":"The twins are where Krishna is established. Let your mind's sorrow go; we are Kshatriyas, bull among men. This daughter of yours has gone like a lotus plant from one pond to another."}},{"n":11,"text":"इति तथ्यं महाराज सर्वमेतद्ब्रवीमि ते ।\nभवान्हि गुरुरस्माकं परमं च परायणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All this, great king, I tell you as it is true; for you are our teacher and our highest refuge."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"ततः स द्रुपदो राजा हर्षव्याकुललोचनः ।\nप्रतिवक्तुं तदा युक्तं नाशकत्तं युधिष्ठिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Drupada, his eyes confused with joy, could not at once give a fitting answer to Yudhishthira."}},{"n":13,"text":"यत्नेन तु स तं हर्षं संनिगृह्य परंतपः ।\nअनुरूपं ततो राजा प्रत्युवाच युधिष्ठिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But the scorcher of foes, controlling that joy with effort, then gave Yudhishthira a fitting reply."}},{"n":14,"text":"पप्रच्छ चैनं धर्मात्मा यथा ते प्रद्रुताः पुरा ।\nस तस्मै सर्वमाचख्यावानुपूर्व्येण पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The righteous king asked him how they had fled in the past, and the Pandava told him everything in order."}},{"n":15,"text":"तच्छ्रुत्वा द्रुपदो राजा कुन्तीपुत्रस्य भाषितम् ।\nविगर्हयामास तदा धृतराष्ट्रं जनेश्वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the son of Kunti's account, King Drupada then denounced the ruler Dhritarashtra."}},{"n":16,"text":"आश्वासयामास च तं कुन्तीपुत्रं युधिष्ठिरम् ।\nप्रतिजज्ञे च राज्याय द्रुपदो वदतां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drupada, best of speakers, comforted Yudhishthira, son of Kunti, and promised him the kingdom."}},{"n":17,"text":"ततः कुन्ती च कृष्णा च भीमसेनार्जुनावपि ।\nयमौ च राज्ञा संदिष्टौ विविशुर्भवनं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Kunti, Krishna, Bhimasena, Arjuna and the twins, as the king bade, entered the great palace."}},{"n":18,"text":"तत्र ते न्यवसन्राजन्यज्ञसेनेन पूजिताः ।\nप्रत्याश्वस्तांस्ततो राजा सह पुत्रैरुवाच तान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They lived there, king, honoured by Yajnasena. Once they were reassured, the king with his sons spoke to them."}},{"n":19,"text":"गृह्णातु विधिवत्पाणिमद्यैव कुरुनन्दनः ।\nपुण्येऽहनि महाबाहुरर्जुनः कुरुतां क्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drupada said: Let the joy of the Kurus, mighty-armed Arjuna, take her hand according to rule today, on this auspicious day; let him make it so."}},{"n":20,"text":"ततस्तमब्रवीद्राजा धर्मपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nममापि दारसंबन्धः कार्यस्तावद्विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Yudhishthira, son of Dharma, said to him: Lord of the people, I too must be married first."}},{"text":"द्रुपद उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Drupada said:"}},{"n":21,"text":"भवान्वा विधिवत्पाणिं गृह्णातु दुहितुर्मम ।\nयस्य वा मन्यसे वीर तस्य कृष्णामुपादिश ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then you yourself, hero, should take my daughter's hand according to rule, or assign Krishna to whomever you think fit."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":22,"text":"सर्वेषां द्रौपदी राजन्महिषी नो भविष्यति ।\nएवं हि व्याहृतं पूर्वं मम मात्रा विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, Draupadi will be the queen of all of us. This is what my mother said earlier, lord of the people."}},{"n":23,"text":"अहं चाप्यनिविष्टो वै भीमसेनश्च पाण्डवः ।\nपार्थेन विजिता चैषा रत्नभूता च ते सुता ॥","meaning":{"en":"And I am not yet married, nor is Bhimasena the Pandava. This daughter of yours, a jewel, was won by Partha."}},{"n":24,"text":"एष नः समयो राजन्रत्नस्य सहभोजनम् ।\nन च तं हातुमिच्छामः समयं राजसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, this is our agreement: a jewel is shared and enjoyed together, and we do not wish to abandon that agreement, best of kings."}},{"n":25,"text":"सर्वेषां धर्मतः कृष्णा महिषी नो भविष्यति ।\nआनुपूर्व्येण सर्वेषां गृह्णातु ज्वलने करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"By dharma Krishna will be the queen of us all; let her take the hand of each of us in turn at the fire."}},{"text":"द्रुपद उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Drupada said:"}},{"n":26,"text":"एकस्य बह्व्यो विहिता महिष्यः कुरुनन्दन ।\nनैकस्या बहवः पुंसो विधीयन्ते कदाचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Many queens are ordained for one man, joy of the Kuru line, but never many men for one woman."}},{"n":27,"text":"लोकवेदविरुद्धं त्वं नाधर्मं धार्मिकः शुचिः ।\nकर्तुमर्हसि कौन्तेय कस्मात्ते बुद्धिरीदृशी ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are righteous and pure, son of Kunti; you should not do an unrighteous thing against the world and the Veda. How has such a thought come to you?"}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":28,"text":"सूक्ष्मो धर्मो महाराज नास्य विद्मो वयं गतिम् ।\nपूर्वेषामानुपूर्व्येण यातं वर्त्मानुयामहे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dharma is subtle, great king, and we do not know its course. We follow the path the elders have taken in order."}},{"n":29,"text":"न मे वागनृतं प्राह नाधर्मे धीयते मतिः ।\nएवं चैव वदत्यम्बा मम चैव मनोगतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"My speech has never uttered falsehood, and my mind is not set on unrighteousness. This is what my mother says, and it is what my own heart says."}},{"n":30,"text":"एष धर्मो ध्रुवो राजंश्चरैनमविचारयन् ।\nमा च तेऽत्र विशङ्का भूत्कथंचिदपि पार्थिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is established dharma, king; practise it without hesitation. Let you have no doubt about it in any way, king."}},{"text":"द्रुपद उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Drupada said:"}},{"n":31,"text":"त्वं च कुन्ती च कौन्तेय धृष्टद्युम्नश्च मे सुतः ।\nकथयन्त्वितिकर्तव्यं श्वः काले करवामहे ॥","meaning":{"en":"You, Kunti, and my son Dhrishtadyumna, son of Kunti, should speak and decide what is to be done; tomorrow we will act at the proper time."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":32,"text":"ते समेत्य ततः सर्वे कथयन्ति स्म भारत ।\nअथ द्वैपायनो राजन्नभ्यागच्छद्यदृच्छया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then they all met and spoke, Bharata, and just then Dvaipayana came there by chance, king."}}]}]}